  "narrative": "No new validation response was released, assessments_due is empty, and the voluntary validation budget is exhausted (remaining_new_requests=0). I therefore made no new accept/reject evidence changes; I only closed two deferred low-priority active claims: H237 (media 5% vs 2%, redundant with prior near-null serum contrasts) and H241 (sparse PTEN-loss by aneuploidy interaction in the clean Avana MSI-negative partition). Direction convention for reading estimates is unchanged: direction +1 positive signed estimates mean higher or less-negative dependency_composite; direction -1 positive signed estimates mean lower or more-negative dependency_composite, i.e. stronger dependency. The outcome threshold for scientific meaningfulness is 0.15 absolute composite units, judged with uncertainty.\n\nSupported findings in this supplied dataset: TP53_loss is robustly associated with higher or less-negative dependency_composite, about +0.80 to +0.84 signed units; KEAP1_loss is similarly robust, about +0.77 to +0.85; SMARCA4_loss is robustly associated with lower or more-negative dependency_composite, about +0.78 to +0.82 for the registered -1 direction; MSI_high is robustly associated with lower or more-negative dependency_composite, about +0.74 to +0.89, with internal validation support (e.g., H85 R52, H86 R65, H107 R78). PTEN_loss is a moderate, partially validated association with stronger dependency, broadly about +0.24 to +0.34, and is stable in clean Avana MSI-negative strata (e.g., H121 R107, H200 R180, H208 R183, H219 R195), with validation support in several broader or high-quality strata (e.g., H26 R38, H125 R105, H132 R92).\n\nNegative or non-threshold findings: CDKN2A_loss should not be reported as an independent threshold-level predictor here; overall and cleaner strata are near threshold or imprecise (e.g., H8 R8/R13, H228 R204, H240 R215). Lineage subtype, sex, research signatures/markers, KRAS, MYC amplification, EGFR amplification, ERBB2 amplification, BRAF, PIK3CA, APC, SMAD4, NF1, RB1, BRCA2, MTAP, ARID1A, dominant library indicators, and serum-media contrasts did not support threshold-level differences in registered directions (e.g., H1 R1, H2 R2, H9 R9, H10 R10, H11 R11, H12 R12, H4 R4, H7 R7, H46 R172, H47 R173, H57 R174, H226 R202). Formal interaction tests generally did not establish scientifically meaningful effect modification, including by ploidy, aneuploidy, mutation burden, lineage, library, MSI status, MYC expression, growth rate, Cas9 activity, EMT, hypoxia, stemness, Wnt activity, research features, and high screen quality for TP53/KEAP1 losses (e.g., H32 R26, H34 R27, H75 R48, H144 R108, H145 R109, H146 R110/R119, H152 R115, H167 R128, H218 R194, H222 R198, H242 R216, H243 R217).\n\nRecent technical checks are reassuring: screen-batch differences and matched omics/Cas9 QC completeness were not threshold-level either broadly or in the biologically cleaner Avana driver-negative MSI-negative partition (H230-H236), reducing but not eliminating concern about technical confounding or selection.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty: the PTEN-loss boundary remains context-dependent at sparse ploidy/aneuploidy partitions (H74, H151, H173, H207, H229, H238-H239); many co-driver strata remain imprecisely positive or invalid; and residual causal confounding cannot be excluded. The most informative next analysis is not more marginal subgroup fishing but a joint model or stratified adjusted contrast that simultaneously includes TP53_loss, KEAP1_loss, SMARCA4_loss, PTEN_loss, MSI_high, ploidy/aneuploidy, mutation burden, screen quality, library, growth pattern, omics/QC status, and interactions among them. This would clarify whether PTEN_loss remains threshold-level after mutual adjustment and whether any apparent context modification is real or a selection/collider artifact.\n\nAll conclusions are associations within this supplied dataset and its internal partitions; they are not causal, not single-gene knockout claims, and not externally generalizable without further validation.",
  "research_notes": "Final ledger notes. No new validation response; validation quota exhausted. Closed H237 and H241 as deferred, not evidence-based scientific rejections. Direction convention: +1 positive = higher/less-negative dependency_composite; -1 positive = lower/more-negative dependency_composite. Threshold 0.15 absolute units. Supported: TP53_loss +0.80 to +0.84; KEAP1_loss +0.77 to +0.85; SMARCA4_loss -1 direction +0.78 to +0.82; MSI_high -1 direction +0.74 to +0.89 with validation; PTEN_loss moderate -1 direction +0.24 to +0.34 with validation in broad/high-quality strata but context-specific sparse estimates unresolved. Not supported: CDKN2A as threshold-level predictor; lineage, sex, research signatures/markers, common driver mutations, library/media nuisance, and most interaction tests. Technical checks: screen batch and matched QC null in broad and clean partitions reduce technical confounding concern. Next: joint adjusted modeling of accepted drivers plus ploidy/aneuploidy, mutation burden, screen quality, library, growth pattern, QC, and interactions; avoid marginal subgroup fishing. All are supplied-dataset associations, not causal or generalizable."
}
